	"description": [
		"This course provides an introduction to the structure and creation of computer software, using the C++ programming language and emphasizing object-oriented programming and structured collaborative software-development methodology. Concepts and skills are applied in a substantial multi-week team project. Topics include object-oriented programming, specification, programmed memory management, indirect addressing, tools including team software process, software design strategies, and elementary ethical analysis of software systems. Offered each semester. Prerequisite: CSCI 221 or permission of instructor."
	],
